# LIBRARY: own
# f2 = told, f3 = paid. A call of what is no built-in closes the turn anyhow: a second copy of the loop for the sites of its reads buys nothing there and costs its operations once more: that loop is walked once.
# RUN(ONCE): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# ONCE-LABEL: code f2:Body
# ONCE-NOT: = GetValueAtSiteOrAbsent
# RUN(TWICE): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# TWICE-LABEL: code f3:Body
# TWICE: = GetValueAtSiteOrAbsent {{*}}key="price"
# TWICE: = Add {{*}}form=Numbers
# RUN: run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# CHECK: 4.5
# CHECK-NEXT: 4.5
# CHECK-NEXT: 3
# CHECK-NEXT: exited with 0
